course: dictionary
lesson: 8977
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Siphon can be a noun, a thing, or a verb, an action. A siphon is a bent tube. To siphon is to move liquid through that tube, or to take things away bit by bit.
explain: «A squid moves fast by jet propulsion: it squirts water out through a funnel called a siphon and shoots the other way.» Here a siphon is a part of the squid's body, a tube that squirts water out. The clues are squirts and water, which show it is a tube in an animal, not a machine.
explain: Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence? Put your meaning into the sentence in place of the word and check that it still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A siphon is a bent tube that moves liquid from a higher container to a lower one, over an edge, without a pump, once the tube is full.
fact: To siphon means to move liquid this way.
fact: Some animals, like squids and clams, have a siphon: a tube they use to suck in or squirt out water.
fact: To siphon off money or resources means to take them away bit by bit, often secretly or wrongly.
fact: Never siphon petrol by mouth, because petrol is poisonous.
exercise: Emptying a fish tank with a hose uses a siphon. What is a siphon? | A bucket with a handle | *A bent tube that moves liquid from a higher place to a lower place, without a pump | A type of fish | A pump with a motor
exercise: «Ravi began to siphon money from the club funds, a little at a time.» What does siphon mean here? | To shine brightly | To grow tall | To pour water into a pond | *To take away bit by bit, often wrongly
exercise: «A squid moves fast by jet propulsion: it squirts water out through a funnel called a siphon.» What does the squid use its siphon for? | *To squirt water out and shoot the other way | To sing loudly | To climb rocks | To catch fish with its arms
test: «Dad used a hose to siphon water out of the paddling pool.» What is the action here? | To freeze the water | *To move water out through a tube | To fill the pool with a bucket | To paint the hose
test: Why should you never siphon petrol by mouth? | It turns the tube red | *Petrol is poisonous | It makes the hose too heavy | Petrol is too cold to swallow
exam: Maya says siphon can only mean a tube. Is she right? | *No, it can also mean to move liquid through a tube, or to take things away bit by bit | Yes, it is a kind of fruit | No, it is only a sound a squid makes | Yes, it is only ever a tube in a fish tank
